            "review_text": "RonTang\nSingapore, Singapore534 contributions\n0\nCold Banh Khot\nDec 2025 • Solo\nThe restaurant is clean and tidy. Staff are helpful even if they speak and understand just a little English. I ordered the mixed Banh Khot (fish, minced pork, and prawn) and a lemon juice. The food came quickly, to my surprise. And no wonder so as the Banh Khot served to me were not warm. Just wondering for how long have they been resting around since they were cooked. The vegetables for wrapping the Banh Khot were fresh and generous, as in most food establishments in Vietnam. The lemon juice was just ok, only a little lemony. Although it wasn’t mentioned in the menu, my mixed Banh Khot came with squid as well. But although it was listed as fish, it is actually fishball. Although not warm, the Banh Khot tasted alright. I’m going to look for Banh Khot at another eatery where they serve them hot from the pan. Do look out for another review of mine about Banh Khot.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nIf you like your food served hot, you’d definitely want to go somewhere else.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 16, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-03",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
